{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>You shall not consent to him.</b> When he says that you should investigate to determine whether his words are true — that such-and-such idolatry is beneficial and such-and-such is harmful." "<b>And you shall not listen to him.</b> In this manner you shall not listen to him and shall not accept from him anything to practice. For if there arises in you any doubt whether it is fitting, you will end up listening to him — because such a doubt arises only from lack of contemplation of the greatness of El, blessed be He, and of His order in the world."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:21.706545385Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}